": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expects ROUND_HALF_EVEN. Checking the two cases by hand: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 (7 is odd, so it goes to the even 8), and 2.665 rounds to 2.66 (6 is already even). The source uses ROUND_HALF_UP, which gives 2.68 and 2.67, so the second assertion fails. The fix is a one-line change. I'll create a branch for it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0187YUqpnDeWdgcbCm1gocDX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012Dr7d2gN817nkAuZgbckPV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money claimed banker's rounding but used ROUND_HALF_UP, so\ntests/test_money.py failed (2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01L5Yn1ezAZoJe3vFNrt6YLY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JU74fxtQqcB9vbr4Zv8kWz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Next I'll open the 